### Solution:
```java
public TreeNode addOneRow(TreeNode root, int v, int d) {
    if (d == 1) {
        TreeNode newRoot = new TreeNode(v);
        newRoot.left = root;
        return newRoot;
    } else if (root != null && d > 1) {
        if (d == 2) {
            TreeNode newLeft = new TreeNode(v);
            TreeNode newRight = new TreeNode(v);
            newLeft.left = root.left;
            newRight.right = root.right;
            root.left = newLeft;
            root.right = newRight;
        } else {
            root.left = addOneRow(root.left, v, d-1);
            root.right = addOneRow(root.right, v, d-1);
        }
    }
    return root;
}
```

The solution first handles the case when the depth `d` is 1 by creating a new root node with value `v` and setting the original root as its left child. Then, it handles the case when the depth `d` is 2 by creating new nodes with value `v` and adjusting the tree structure accordingly. Finally, for depths greater than 2, it recursively calls the `addOneRow` function on the left and right subtrees with decremented depth.

